# Quality

`quality/rules.py` holds hard validity checks. Failures are quarantined with a
typed error code (`SCHEMA_INVALID`, `TEMPERATURE_PHYSICALLY_IMPOSSIBLE`,
`IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT`, and the other codes in that module).

`quality/signals.py` holds operational signals: stale sensors, sequence gaps,
environmental-limit violations, equipment-state inconsistencies. Those rows
stay in Silver.

Do not move a signal check into a quarantine error code.
